# This repository is rooted at $HOME, not at ~/etc/dotfiles. Every cache,
# browser profile, SDK and node_modules under the home directory is therefore a
# candidate for `git add -A`: 1,501,557 untracked files before this file existed,
# including agent transcripts that embed live API keys. Until the root moves
# (see "Repo Hygiene" in etc/secrets/TODO.md), the posture here is
# deny-by-default — ignore everything at the top level, then re-admit only the
# paths that actually hold tracked content.
#
# Consequence: a genuinely new top-level path needs `git add -f`, or a new
# negation below. That friction is the point.

/*

!/.gitignore
!/.gitmodules
!/.stowrc
!/.xsession
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/NOTES.md
!/README.md
!/TODO.md
!/bin/
!/etc/
!/lib/
!/notes/
!/plans/
!/prg/
!/var/

# Pre-existing rules.
.aider*
.serena/

# ~/.pi is a stow-folded symlink to etc/dotfiles/dot-pi, so everything the
# agent writes at runtime lands inside git: session transcripts with full `env`
# dumps (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, ROBLOSECURITY, GitHub PATs, Postgres DSNs),
# auth.json, and OAuth tokens under mcp-oauth/. Same deny-by-default trick, so
# anything new the agent drops here is ignored until it is explicitly admitted.
/etc/dotfiles/dot-pi/agent/*
!/etc/dotfiles/dot-pi/agent/keybindings.json
!/etc/dotfiles/dot-pi/agent/mcp.json
!/etc/dotfiles/dot-pi/agent/models.json
!/etc/dotfiles/dot-pi/agent/settings.json

# Installed artifacts and package-manager caches inside admitted trees. Nothing
# under these is tracked (var/racket: 0 tracked / 24,222 files; var/web: 0 / 701).
# The emacs entries are package managers, byte-cache and fetched state — the 7
# tracked .el files sit directly in dot-emacs.d/, not in these subdirectories.
/var/racket/
/var/web/
/etc/dotfiles/dot-emacs.d/straight/
/etc/dotfiles/dot-emacs.d/elpaca/
/etc/dotfiles/dot-emacs.d/elpa/
/etc/dotfiles/dot-emacs.d/eln-cache/
/etc/dotfiles/dot-emacs.d/backups/
/etc/dotfiles/dot-emacs.d/auto-save-list/
/etc/dotfiles/dot-emacs.d/tree-sitter/
/etc/dotfiles/dot-emacs.d/url/
